# Infrastructure

Sources of truth: [docs/environments.md](../../docs/environments.md), [docs/observability.md](../../docs/observability.md)

- Cloud Run is the canonical deployment target. Workers and VPS/Docker are alternatives, not the default CI path.
- All secrets live in Secret Manager (or Workers Secrets); no `.env` files committed.
- CI deploys via Workload Identity Federation; long-lived service-account keys in repo secrets are forbidden.
- Container base: `node:22-bookworm-slim`, runs as non-root, listens on `$PORT`.
- Image promotion is digest-based — never rebuild between staging and prod.
- Logs are `pino` JSON with required fields: `request_id`, `session_id_hash`, `outcome`, `latency_ms`, plus tool/drive context where applicable.
- Redaction config covers `authorization`, `cookie`, `access_token`, `refresh_token`, `code`, `id_token`. PRs that touch OAuth must re-verify the redaction list.
- Alerts: `tools.list.empty` (page), `oauth.refresh_failure` >1% (page), `cloud_run_5xx` >1% (page), p95 latency >3 s (warn), secret-in-log canary (page).
- Each pageable alert has a runbook in `docs/runbooks/`.
